runtime: authenticate live shutdown socket retirement

Pin the private directory and control socket inode while authenticating
a live stop request. Retire only that unchanged socket after the same
runner and launch have complete exit proof, including every recorded child.
This permits final-controller shutdown of a genuine K68 runner that leaves
its control socket without granting later dead-residual recovery authority.

Use the final controller for predecessor stop, then preserve genuine K68
resume and final-controller live update in the direct verifier.
